# Parallel Slice Hygiene & Migration Governance

## Parallel Agent Isolation
- Check `docs/migration/STATUS.md` and `gh pr list --label migration` before claiming a slice so two agents never collide on the same slice or crate.
- Never run `git stash`, `git reset --hard`, or cherry-pick/merge commits from another agent's branch or worktree.
- Commit only files belonging to your claimed slice.

## Feature Flags & Safe Rollback
- Gate every migrated slice behind its feature flag (`legacy` | `rust-wasm` | `gpui-native` | `shadow`).
- Always keep `prod` defaulted to `legacy` in `packages/desktop/src/shared/flags/environments.json` until explicit human rollout approval.
- Verify `flag=legacy` rollback renders cleanly and leaves existing `preferences.json` and markdown files 100% intact.

## Oracle Protection & Review Gate
- Never delete, skip, or relax existing unit/E2E/conformance tests, stub failing functions, or apply CI waiver labels.
- Never commit PR screenshots or recordings into tracked git paths; keep them in `/tmp/` or `/opt/cursor/artifacts/`.
- Always target `develop`, tag `@shashu10` for human review, and **never self-merge**.
